<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.pool.lays ~ init ~ one git working tree per pool, idempotent

`lares surface init` makes the worn (or `--face N`) face's root at `projections/faces/<pet name>/` a pool: `.git` at 0700, the house's ignore list, a local author `<pet name> <slug>@face.invalid` and a pre-commit pool-check hook. It changes only what does not already stand as the house writes it, and a second run says already. `--realm <realm pet name>` makes the realm's root its one pool under the realm's identity, never a face's, lifting any tree nested below it with its history kept, and each share row's workspace a pool under its wiki's identity; a wiki whose folder stands nowhere yet reads unlaid. `--workspace <name>` makes a bound workspace folder a pool under a workspace author. It runs on this machine; with no LAR_ROOT it reads the container house's pools under LARES_HOUSE.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ face · realm · workspace

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`face` params=`~ the worn face's root becomes its pool`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`realm` params=`realm/notes ~ the realm's one tree and its workspaces`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`workspace` params=`workspace/garden ~ a bound workspace folder`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

